  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「アカキナノキ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%A2%E3%82%AB%E3%82%AD%E3%83%8A%E3%83%8E%E3%82%AD",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 110689681,
      "text": "アカキナノキ はアカネ科に属する木本の一種。マラリアの特効薬であるキニーネを生産する。世界の侵略的外来種ワースト100に選定されている。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Cinchona pubescens」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinchona_pubescens",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1369965711,
      "text": "Cinchona pubescens, also known as red cinchona and quina or kina, is native to Central and South America. It is known as a medicinal plant for its bark's high quinine content- and has similar uses to C. officinalis in the production of quinine, most famously used for treatment of malaria."
    }
